# DHI-11 V6 — Complexity-First Orris-Led — Pour Card

**Completed development card — 2026-09-06. NOT COMPOUNDED. Physical compounding / skin use / safety / release: HOLD.**

33 stock rows • 6,000 µL raw-stock concentrate • 24,000 µL Ethanol 96% • nominal 30 mL. “20%” means raw-stock v/v under additive-volume convention, not neat odorants or w/w.

DHI 2011 is the target; DHP 2025 supplies the structural method. Irotyl is excluded. This is a new batch, NOT a V5 bottle addition. The four-part iris nucleus is unchanged. Ten extra rows test target-linked relationships; they do not prove more perceived layers.

## Before using this card

Use the exact stocks below. Orris 9% w/w DEP, Alpha Irone 10% w/w DEP, Ambrettolide 10% w/w DPG and Tonkarome 20% w/w TEC are not interchangeable with similarly named volume-fraction or differently diluted stocks. All other selected rows are neat/as supplied. Carrot Seed, Cedramber and Cashmeran must be the selected NEAT principal stocks, despite stale runtime dilution display labels.

Stock IDs, provenance and qualification limits are in [the canonical V6 design](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/formulas/DHI-11_V6_Complexity_First_Orris_Led_30mL_20pct.design.json). Record actual delivered stock masses; do not treat µL × w/w fraction as measured active volume. Exact ppm and blend safety cannot yet be certified. Orris/Tonkarome composition and the formal DHP donor gate remain unresolved.

