## Separate final diluent

| Solvent | Planned transfer |
|---|---:|
| Ethanol 96% | 24,000 µL |

**Nominal total: 30,000 µL.** Do not add the model's ethanol/water constituents again. Contraction, evaporation and transfer loss are unmeasured.

Minimum listed raw transfer: 10 µL. No direct solid dosing is authorized. If any stock is not a homogeneous pipettable liquid at handling conditions, stop and qualify it; do not guess a preparation. Do not scale every row down for a smaller bottle. After qualification, an aliquot of a properly prepared master concentrate can avoid sub-10 µL individual additions.

Use appropriate SDS handling, ventilation and ignition control. This card does not authorize skin testing, heating, commercial release or a claim of stability. It gives planned transfers, not evidence that a perfume was physically compounded.

## Verification and sensory boundary

**Artifact and regression checks:** 86 passed, 0 failed. These verify software records and arithmetic, not physical smell or safety.

**Current diagnostic:** 108 PASS / 34 WARN / 3 FAIL / 1 SKIP. All 33 exact stock bindings and the V5-to-V6 dose guard PASS; overall release remains HOLD. The failures are missing Orris composite evidence, Tonkarome opacity, and aggregate preflight. Formal DHP donor-independence is separately NOT RUN / HOLD. [Full warning diagnosis and learnings](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/formulas/DHI-11_V6_Complexity_First_VERIFICATION_AND_LEARNINGS.md).

The fixed table and stock bindings are available now. Current numerical diagnostics are attached to [the master formula](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/formulas/DHI-11_V6_Complexity_First_Orris_Led_30mL_20pct.md); the machine-readable status is in [the V6 design record](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/formulas/DHI-11_V6_Complexity_First_Orris_Led_30mL_20pct.design.json). Regardless of a software pass, the physical release state remains HOLD.

Ten proposed modules / seven connections are design hypotheses. The critical next sensory questions are whether the cold root and warm cream remain simultaneously legible, whether iris survives at distance, and whether the third musk earns its role. [Controlled-trial sheet](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/formulas/DHI-11_V6_Complexity_First_CONTROLLED_TRIAL.md).
